WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.880
I have more than comfortable putting loads of meat in my mouth. I was excited!

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.300
He's more of a hovering than soaring gracefully, but it'll do.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.840
Yay, I love finding severed body parts...! :D

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.940
*panting* I DO NOT SUPPORT ANIMAL CRUELTY! *not sponsered by PETA*

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:24.420
- You've been the best friend I could ask for. 
- I love you.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:25.580
- Love you too, Ro.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:33.620
A theory about a show I'm in, where I play myself, but also a detective from the 1970s?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.980
That would be meta enough, but get this:

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.300
The show, Escape the Night,

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.980
actually sponsored this video and approved me talking about how the show's host

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:44.160
is actually evil and can't be trusted.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.140
The level of meta in this episode has just hit a brand new extreme!

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.490
Hello, Internet!

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.560
Welcome to Film Theory!

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.860
A true YouTube original.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.010
Not like an official show produced by YouTube "YouTube original"

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.579
I just mean an original series only found here on YouTube.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.620
You know what IS a show produced by YouTube however?

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:21.912
Escape the Night.

00:01:21.912 --> 00:01:25.440
the longest-running YouTube original series of all time.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.780
Which, ironically enough, also has the longest tagline for a show of all time.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.880
According to the show's trailer, Escape the Night is a...

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.280
Thing's like a Mad Libs on steroids.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.840
Yes, YouTube, I too can throw adjectives into a blender and make them appear on screen in fancy graphics.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.880
Film Theory is YouTube's

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.520
Slap that on a t-shirt and sell it!

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.940
But, for as much as I joke, Escape the Night is, at its core, something all us theorists love:

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:06.960
a mystery.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:13.140
A super-sized horror themed escape room where, every step along the way, a popular YouTuber dies.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.520
Being on the show is almost like a YouTuber rite of passage at this point.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:21.180
For some of the biggest creators on the platform showing up to prove their puzzle-solving prowess.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.860
Season one had the likes of GloZell, Lele Pons and Shane Dawson,

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:28.080
Season two featured Tana Mongeau, Liza Koshy and Gabbie Hanna,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:28.980
and season three...

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.560
the best season cuz it's my season...

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.580
had a ton of my favorite people both on and off YouTube,

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:39.440
Like Colleen Ballinger, Safiya Nygaard and my sister from another mister Rosanna Pansino.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.840
And now season four, the newest season which launches today,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:46.440
promises to feature the best of the best, as it's an all-star season.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.900
I mean, how you doing an all-star season when canonically everyone is dead is beyond me,

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.840
but then again, I was dead too at one point 
and I got revived so...

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.260
look at me setting the trends!

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.880
#DeadAndLovingIt

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.880
But here's the thing, even though Escape the Night is like

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:01.830
the bizarre love child of Survivor and 
American Horror Story,

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:06.700
where people get voted out, and instead of torches getting snuffed out by a smarmy host,

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.920
it's your life getting snuffed out by a bloodthirsty harpy.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.480
There is a deeper lore present throughout this entire thing.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:16.680
This isn't just a competition reality show,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.740
there is a massive story that spans all three seasons of this thing.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.220
A story that most viewers, heck even us contestants,

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.520
aren't aware of, because it's so well hidden.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.640
Don't believe me? Here's a great example:

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.360
See this arm from season one?

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.840
Seems like just any old creepy clue right?

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.920
WRONG! Notice the patterns on the arm,

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:40.760
which matches up to our mentor Calliope's arm tattoos from season three.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:42.900
The two are connected.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.700
At the end of our season, Calliope dies,

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.300
and, somehow, her arm ends up back at the haunted house the YouTubers explore in season one.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.580
There are tons of little details just like this sprinkled throughout the show,

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.440
all pointing to the larger series narrative.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.180
And, as I've gone back through to rebinge the series in time for the show's return,

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.700
and the return of some of my dearly departed friends,

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.860
something is now isn't clear to me.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:10.400
Something that I suspected during my season, that I now see beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.100
The host and show's creator, popular Youtube vlogger Joey Graceffa

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:18.400
is actually the villain of his own series.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.680
Even though he acts just like any other contestant,

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:25.540
fighting whatever murderous clowns or bloodthirsty robots the show throws your way that week,

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:29.040
he's one of them, working against us.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.780
He's a plant, a villain, someone out to sabotage his friends.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.560
And the craziest part of all,

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.560
is that he might not even recognize it.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:43.280
Beware, my friends. Going forward, the tea gets hot, and plot lines start getting a little bit spoiler-y

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.160
so consider yourself warned

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.680
To understand the plot of the series and the role Joey plays

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.180
in bringing about the deaths of dozens of popular online personalities

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.240
We need to know where things began.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:06.200
Season one opens with Joey explaining that he's having weird dreams when he suddenly inherits a large estate.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:10.760
He accepts it on blind faith and as if he hasn't seen the plot of any horror movie in existence ever,

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.280
promptly decides to move in.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:15.800
He claims: "it won't let me sleep until I invite others"

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:20.940
And instead of being like "huh, that's a red flag, maybe I should consider posting up at the Comfort Inn instead"

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:23.780
He thinks that his insomnia will be cured if he throws a party.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:27.180
All of this is very logical decision making from Joey

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:31.430
Moving into the meet of episode 1 it's revealed that the king of conspiracy theories himself

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.960
Shane Dawson has been poisoned at dinner and dies

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:37.940
Whoopsy there goes Shane's next docu-series darn it

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.560
and I had already pre-ordered my conspiracy theory makeup palette

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.420
They come to learn that Shane was actually a member of a secret society

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:47.840
creatively named the Society Against Evil.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:53.080
which is, get this, a society that fights against evil.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.100
Truth in advertising for the win.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.720
The house that Joey's inherited is possessed by an evil spirit

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.060
and the gang has to find a bunch of hidden artifacts,

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:03.100
bring them all together and free themselves with a ritual

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.780
The Society Against Evil has marked clues around the house to help them

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.660
and season one progresses as contestants get bumped off

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:13.280
and Joey gets closer and closer to his fully ghost busted dream home

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:17.740
The problem is Joey doesn't exactly show himself to be on the good guys side.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:22.400
As the season goes on we see Joey playing along as though he's helping to rid the house of demons

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.000
But if you actually stop and look at his behavior

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.920
things just don't add up.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:31.640
Take for instance this scene where Joey and Lele Pons uncover a Death Note

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:35.360
which gives them the opportunity to kill off one of their friends by writing down their name

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:39.180
Lily suggests that they give the decision up to fate by playing spin the bottle

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:43.140
Joey however insists that they write down GloZell.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:45.980
Not only one of the most popular players in the house

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.640
but also one of the most vocal in her suspicions

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:52.020
of Joey's role in all the murder that's happening around them

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:55.240
"We buried Justine, but you were acting like you were just so sad

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.260
and I just don't believe that you're really so sad"

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:00.060
- Why
- I don't buy the act at all, Joey.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.200
"GloZell was going in at Joey...

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.740
and now Joey's killed GloZell. Why?"

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.260
Joey's rationale for making such a cruel choice?

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.620
"It was either her or me"

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:10.820
Lele pretty much has to go along with the decision

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.160
"well, it is your house, so..."

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:17.820
but if that wasn't suspicious enough, Joey then proceeds to cover up his role in GloZell's murder

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:20.020
"I don't want them to know that we put her name in the book"

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:24.160
Making up a lie, and repeatedly pressuring Lele about keeping the secret

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.840
And is Joey sorry about his decision?

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:35.100
Does he regret killing off not only a friend but also one of the most beloved members of his party?

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.220
I'll let him speak for himself

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.520
"It's my party and I can kill whoever I want to"

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.420
The two other people who are suspicious of him

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:45.860
but keep it under wraps also happened to be the final survivors of the season

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:51.560
So Joey invites his friends to a party and then shows zero remorse as he kills them off one at a time

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:57.240
No big deal, right? I mean it is, but the goal is to escape this house possessed by an evil spirit

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.400
so I guess it kinda makes sense

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:03.460
Except again, there's one huge problem with Joey's behavior

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:06.740
Joey keeps the house at the end of the season.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:12.360
Let me make that clear: he pockets the deed to a murder house possessed by evil spirits.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.100
An act that he clearly knows is wrong

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:19.170
because he secretly does it outside of the sight of the other surviving YouTubers

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:22.480
I mean, Joey, I know LA real estate is cutthroat, man,

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:28.600
I live here too, but there's no excuse for holding onto a property that's literally killed eight of your BFFs

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:34.180
"I don't think anyone will understand what happened tonight at this house."

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.760
That's right, Joey, they won't.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.940
They think that you heroically escaped with your life.

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:41.700
But what really happened is that you racked up a death toll of eight

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:44.980
in exchange for some real estate straight out of the Shining.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:47.300
Even the other survivors aren't fooled

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:52.020
When he asks them back for his next dinner party in season two their response says it all

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:55.980
*agressively* "I am not going to another party by Joey"

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.360
"Not today, Satan"

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:02.660
By season two, we see that the evil that's possessed the house is now creeping into Joey himself.

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:05.040
You can even see it start to show up on his face.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:08.820
At no point does he, you know, asked for help or told anyone like

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:12.400
"Hey, guys! Joey here. I think I might have the touch of the curse going on"

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:15.840
That would be a kick-by YouTube video Joey, but did you do it? Nope.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:19.720
Over the course of the season the next crop of dead men and women walking

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:21.900
worked their way through a Victorian masquerade

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:26.340
where they fend off everything from the king of vampires to an evil gingerbread woman.

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:32.500
Along the way we yet again see Joey betraying the very people who are there trying to help him out.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:35.080
When DeStorm calls Joey's team weak.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.740
"I think Joey's team is weak"

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.660
"Slow, can't keep up with us"

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:42.100
Joey immediately responds by cutting his throat

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:50.820
And Joey's wrath isn't just limited to people who question him.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.980
He even sacrifices people from his own alliances.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:58.160
In episode 1 Joey and Liza Koshi are chained to sacrificial crosses

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.260
destined to be food for vampires.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:03.760
They escape and from that moment on they are practically inseparable.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:07.820
As you can imagine almost becoming an undead buffet is a way of uniting people

00:10:07.820 --> 00:10:10.380
Until of course Joey decides to turn on Liza.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.160
"I feel like Liza could handle it"

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:18.520
"What is this about? Joey and I had a great time being a great team and now he wants to send me to my death?"

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:23.020
Unfortunately, the remaining players are just so happy to be alive that they don't call him out on it

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.220
so Joey slips by until the next episode.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:31.580
Here finally Joey has to actually fight for his own life after being unanimously nominated by his team

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:35.160
"The only two that haven't proven themselves yet are Joey and Andrea"

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:39.340
After completing the challenge for the second time in this series

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:43.380
Joey has to choose someone outside of the challenge to die

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:49.060
And after about ten seconds of being distraught about it, he chooses Tana Mongeau,

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:52.700
and then he's mad that he didn't get himself a power gem in return.

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:58.180
"It makes me so angry that Tana just died and we didn't get what we were promised."

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:00.800
Geez, she hasn't even put on TanaCon yet.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:05.040
Joey Graceffa literally cancels Tana before the internet does.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.900
Girl's been canceled more times than Futurama.

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:12.780
By the end of the season Joey has the blood of yet another seven YouTubers on his hands,

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:16.140
but in an interesting twist, he himself dies in the final moments

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:19.820
Unfortunately what is dead may never die because Joey is back at it in season 3

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.060
after making a quick pact with none other

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:23.740
than The Society Against Evil.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:27.960
Which, the more I research the more it seems like their name might be compensating for something,

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:29.940
at this point it's unclear what side they're actually on

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:32.960
but what is clear is that they offered Joey a choice:

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:34.220
he can get his life back

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:39.400
but to do so he'll have to sacrifice the lives of yet another batch of content creators

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:44.360
Joey Graceffa, ladies and gentlemen taking down YouTubers faster than a Mr Beast paintball tournament

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:45.020
"I'm out"

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:47.800
This deal in which he has to trade the lives of others for his own life

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:50.320
is of course a deal that Joey accepts without question

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.160
"if they find out my secret, I'm ruined"

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.480
And this time I'm caught in the crossfire.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:12:00.160
And we were off to the carnival. A carnival from the 1970s to be exact.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:05.020
This time Joey does actually bother to warn everyone that they're headed into a dangerous mission

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:08.960
but you know dangerous is a far cry from certain death

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:12.380
Here I am thinking that I'm finally cool enough to be invited to a YouT uber party,

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:15.240
but instead of collabs I get kill-abs

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:15.960
They kill me

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:26.040
I die. In fact Colleen and I both died directly at Joey's hands

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:31.240
in a pretty suspicious way after we both call him out for you know sacrificing all his friends

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:33.760
so that he and he alone can come back to life.

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:35.000
"You need me"

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:35.920
"Liar"

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.460
"How am I... How is that a..."

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:40.200
"You are a liar, I don't believe anything that you say"

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:41.940
Seems to be a trend across these three seasons, huh?

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:46.460
You see, for the first time in the series we all started to figure out that something was going on

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:48.560
and we decided to call Joey out on it.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:51.660
"Is Joey on our side or is he just trying to kill us?"

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.460
And for the first time in the entire series

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:58.160
Joey comes clean about the fact that his life depends on surviving the season

00:12:58.160 --> 00:12:59.940
"I didn't know what was going on and I'm...

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:05.020
I signed a contract that I would save this town and they would bring me back to life if I don't save this town...

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.420
...

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:07.180
I die with it"

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.600
And yeah, he brings out his little crocodile tears

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:13.900
but the fact of the matter is Joey if you sentenced everyone around you to die

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.520
to make your little behind-the-scenes deal

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:17.300
"I didn't know how you guys would take it"

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.500
"Pretty poorly actually...
(whooah MatPat with the salt)

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:24.680
cuz what you just said is that you're willing to trade nine lives for yours, Joey? Great.

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:26.440
There's no justice here."

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:29.120
Yeeah, you go dorky sheriff MatPat!
(whoot whoot)

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.840
and then like clockwork anytime anyone tries to disagree with Joey,

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:35.540
I end up in the unfortunate position of dying.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:39.120
I fail in a nail-biting tiebreaker against Manny MUA.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:42.480
By the way, can we just take a second to look at what a trihard I am here?

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:46.200
*everyone cheering for MatPat*

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:48.500
Take note reality TV contestants.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.840
This is how you get way too invested it into your character

00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:54.740
Anyway my ego and my life set aside

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:57.480
in the next episode there's an even more blatant betrayal

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.020
after Colleen also calls into question the mighty wisdom of Joey.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:03.820
"Nice acting, Joey. I don't believe any of it.

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.400
He even had a single tear, I swear to god that was a spit tear"

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.800
"One of the biggest things I feel I've done so far was have a gut feeling about Joey"

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:12.680
And then finds herself on the wrong end of his death hammer

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:13.640
"I'm gonna vote for you"

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:16.460
"Joey I'm sorry I came for you earlier but you were lying to us"

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:19.220
And then just to make sure that none of his other secrets get out

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:24.100
Joey makes sure that Colleen ends up in an iron maiden literally screaming and crying

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:26.540
"Please, you guys, please stop, please"

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.520
So at this point in the series it's pretty clear

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:31.500
that Joey leaves a path of heartless deaths in his wake

